DATA QUALITY NOTE — vendor extraction
--------------------------------------
Several items were tagged with vendor token "SEC" (e.g. Brinks Home, Chrome extension story, Thermo
Fisher, water-utility story, Hugging Face Diffusers story) despite having nothing to do with the U.S.
Securities and Exchange Commission or SEC disclosure rules. This looks like a substring-matching bug in
src/normalize.py's vendor extractor — likely matching "sec" inside the word "security", which appears in
nearly every headline in this feed. Treated "SEC" as noise throughout clustering/scoring below (did not
use it as a shared-vendor-token clustering signal, and did not count it toward vendor_match scoring).
Flagging for the user per scope discipline — not fixed in this run.

Separately: N-able (N-central RMM) is not in config/sources.yaml's vendor list, despite RMM/MSP tooling
being squarely relevant to this audience (many resellers are MSPs or serve MSPs directly). Editorial
judgment credited it on severity/brand-breach-adjacent grounds instead of vendor_match. Worth adding
N-able, plus other major RMM/PSA vendors (ConnectWise, Kaseya, Datto, Atera, NinjaOne) to the vendor
list given today's story.

